x264 is GPL-2.0-or-later, not GPL-2.0 alone. OpenSSL 3.0.15 is under the
Apache License 2.0. The license text is licenses/gcast-ffmpeg/Apache-2.0.txt.
FFmpeg's configure requires --enable-version3 when --enable-gpl is combined
with OpenSSL 3, so the helper ffmpeg binary is GPL-3.0-or-later. The GPL-3.0
text is licenses/uxplay/LICENSE. ffprobe is LGPL-2.1-or-later with OpenSSL
(no --enable-gpl). The LGPL-2.1 text is licenses/ffmpeg/COPYING.LGPLv2.1.

Configure lines are in scripts/build_gcast_ffmpeg.sh:

- x264 0480cb05fa188d37ae87e8f4fd8f1aea3711f7ee:
  ./configure --host=arm-none-linux-gnueabihf --cross-prefix=arm-none-linux-gnueabihf- --enable-static --disable-cli --disable-opencl --disable-asm
- FFmpeg 8.1.2 ffmpeg:
  --enable-gpl --enable-version3 --enable-libx264 --enable-openssl --enable-static --disable-shared
- FFmpeg 8.1.2 ffprobe (no libx264):
  --enable-openssl --enable-static --disable-shared --disable-ffmpeg
  (neither configure passes --disable-ffprobe)
